---
title: "5 · Generate and check the draft"
description: Generate the contract, read it through and, if needed, edit the wording for this client.
sidebar:
  order: 12
  label: "5 · Generate and check the draft"
---

**Who:** the person in charge. **Where:** step 2 **Draft**, which opens after **Generate contract** on step 1 (see [4 · Prepare the contract](/en/crm/prepare/)).

{% steps %}

1. After **Generate contract** on step 1, the Draft step opens. The contract received its number when it was first generated (for example SAF-2026-0001), and the PDF opens in the page. A Word copy is saved with it.
2. Read the contract through. The right panel sums up the client, the number, the issuing entity, the template and the totals, and lists the **History** of the contract.
3. Go through the **Checks**: every line has its contract name and wording in the contract's language, whether the discount is within the approval threshold, and whether the client signatory has an email address.

{% /steps %}

{% screenshot id="crm/draft-generated" caption="A generated draft, with download, upload and regenerate." /%}

**Wording printed in this draft** shows, per contract language, each service's name on contract, category title, description and conditions as they were printed. Later changes under **Services & Packages** reach the contract only when it is generated again.

## Change the wording for this client only

{% steps %}

1. Select **Download Word** and edit the file.
2. Keep the signature marks on the signing page. The upload is checked for them.
3. Select **Upload edited draft**, choose the `.docx` file and select **Upload**.

{% /steps %}

If the edited draft has lost a signature mark, choose how to continue: **Put the original signature page back and upload again**, or **Keep this draft and place the signature boxes by hand when sending**.

Do not change prices in Word. An amount changed in Word does not change the contract's amounts. Change them on the **Services** tab and generate the contract again.

## Generate again

**Regenerate** builds the draft again from the current services. If an edited draft was uploaded, you are asked to confirm with **Generate and replace**; the upload stays in the document's version history.

If the **Services** tab changes after the contract was generated, a notice above the step bar lists the changes. Generate the contract again to include them.

{% aside type="caution" title="Edited drafts always need approval" %}
A contract whose draft was edited by hand goes to approval, whatever the discount.
{% /aside %}
